# Caddyfile — sovereign-sigint
#
# Default: plain HTTP on :8000, reverse-proxied to Open WebUI on
# 127.0.0.1:8080. Not port 80: rootless Podman can't bind ports below
# 1024 without lowering net.ipv4.ip_unprivileged_port_start
# system-wide (a real install hit this — "bind: permission denied" on
# :80) — moving Caddy to :8000 avoids a system-wide policy change for
# one container's convenience of a bare URL.
#
# No domain configured, so Caddy's automatic HTTPS is NOT active here
# — that feature requires a real public domain with DNS pointing at
# this box and port 443 reachable from the internet, which doesn't fit
# an internal lab/production box on a LAN.
#
# If/when this needs HTTPS on the LAN:
#   - For a real domain with public DNS: replace ":8000" below with
#     your domain name (e.g. "sigint.example.com") and Caddy will
#     handle Let's Encrypt automatically — no other config needed.
#   - For LAN-only HTTPS with a self-signed cert: use "tls internal"
#     inside the block instead, and trust Caddy's local CA on client
#     machines that need to avoid browser warnings.

:8000 {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
}
